01:05:38.530 --> 01:05:41.200
The next tool is to
improve your fitness are

01:05:41.200 --> 01:05:42.940
psychological tools,
and they're really

01:05:42.940 --> 01:05:45.850
geared toward enhancing your
focus during your workout

01:05:45.850 --> 01:05:48.610
and separating or
segmenting your workouts

01:05:48.610 --> 01:05:50.530
from the other
parts of your day.

01:05:50.530 --> 01:05:52.540
Now, of course,
workouts are naturally

01:05:52.540 --> 01:05:54.370
segmented from the
other parts of your day,

01:05:54.370 --> 01:05:56.560
unless you're running
around all day long,

01:05:56.560 --> 01:05:59.260
or you're lifting weights or
other heavy objects all day

01:05:59.260 --> 01:05:59.960
long.

01:05:59.960 --> 01:06:02.140
But one of the more
attractive tools

01:06:02.140 --> 01:06:04.840
that was presented during
the series with Dr. Galpin

01:06:04.840 --> 01:06:07.990
that I adopted and found
to be really effective

01:06:07.990 --> 01:06:09.910
is this concept of the line.

01:06:09.910 --> 01:06:14.260
The line is this concept that
you have a physical location,

01:06:14.260 --> 01:06:17.590
say at the entrance to a gym
or at the start of your run

01:06:17.590 --> 01:06:20.290
or your bike or maybe it's
around the stationary exercise

01:06:20.290 --> 01:06:24.310
device that you use for which
once you cross that line,

01:06:24.310 --> 01:06:26.320
you are all about business.

01:06:26.320 --> 01:06:26.830
OK.

01:06:26.830 --> 01:06:29.240
You're not socializing
or at least not too much.

01:06:29.240 --> 01:06:30.740
You don't want to
be rude to people,

01:06:30.740 --> 01:06:33.100
but you're really
focused on your workout.

01:06:33.100 --> 01:06:35.230
So this is especially
effective on days

01:06:35.230 --> 01:06:36.850
when you're a little
bit distracted,

01:06:36.850 --> 01:06:38.808
or you didn't sleep that
well the night before,

01:06:38.808 --> 01:06:41.080
or maybe you've got something
going on in your mind,

01:06:41.080 --> 01:06:42.940
or you're in an
argument, or you're

01:06:42.940 --> 01:06:44.322
excited about something else.

01:06:44.322 --> 01:06:46.030
But if you care about
your fitness, which

01:06:46.030 --> 01:06:49.060
I hope everyone does, and
your goal during any workout

01:06:49.060 --> 01:06:50.920
is to stimulate
a particular type

01:06:50.920 --> 01:06:53.380
of physiological adaptation
strength, hypertrophy,

01:06:53.380 --> 01:06:55.190
long-distance
endurance, et cetera,

01:06:55.190 --> 01:06:58.330
and you also don't want to
get injured so that you can

01:06:58.330 --> 01:07:00.940
continue to train
for your entire life

01:07:00.940 --> 01:07:03.820
as regularly as possible,
the concept of the line

01:07:03.820 --> 01:07:06.790
is fantastic
because what it does

01:07:06.790 --> 01:07:09.580
is it forces you
to compartmentalize

01:07:09.580 --> 01:07:12.040
the portion of your lesson
that comes before the workout

01:07:12.040 --> 01:07:15.520
and after the workout and also
to really enjoy your workouts.

01:07:15.520 --> 01:07:17.560
This is something that's
not often discussed,

01:07:17.560 --> 01:07:20.660
but nowadays with the
advent of smartphones,

01:07:20.660 --> 01:07:23.840
there's a lot of infiltration
of other types of communication

01:07:23.840 --> 01:07:27.800
and information while one is
supposed to be exercising.

01:07:27.800 --> 01:07:30.740
And so our life has become
far less compartmentalized

01:07:30.740 --> 01:07:32.990
than it used to be before
the advent of smartphones.

01:07:32.990 --> 01:07:34.740
Now, of course,
smartphones are wonderful.

01:07:34.740 --> 01:07:37.250
They provide all sorts of
wonderful tools and benefits,

01:07:37.250 --> 01:07:38.517
and of course, I use one.

01:07:38.517 --> 01:07:40.100
And I'll talk about
how to incorporate

01:07:40.100 --> 01:07:41.642
the smartphone in
a very specific way

01:07:41.642 --> 01:07:43.710
to enhance your workouts
in just a moment.

01:07:43.710 --> 01:07:45.980
But the idea of a line
is you pick a location.

01:07:45.980 --> 01:07:48.230
It can change with each
workout, but ideally it

01:07:48.230 --> 01:07:51.650
would be at the threshold of
where the physical location

01:07:51.650 --> 01:07:52.730
to the workout begins.

01:07:52.730 --> 01:07:56.180
And once you cross that
line, you are all business.

01:07:56.180 --> 01:07:58.148
You are taking care of business.

01:07:58.148 --> 01:08:00.440
Which is not to say that you
can't enjoy your workouts.

01:08:00.440 --> 01:08:01.760
In fact, you absolutely should.

01:08:01.760 --> 01:08:04.898
One of the best pieces of advice
that I ever got about fitness

01:08:04.898 --> 01:08:06.440
was given to me when
I was a teenager

01:08:06.440 --> 01:08:07.820
and I started lifting weights.

01:08:07.820 --> 01:08:11.840
And the person who was teaching
me how to do that said,

01:08:11.840 --> 01:08:13.880
one of the best
things that you can do

01:08:13.880 --> 01:08:17.660
and you absolutely should do
for your fitness now and forever

01:08:17.660 --> 01:08:20.399
is to learn to
enjoy training hard.

01:08:20.399 --> 01:08:21.660
And that really stuck with me.

01:08:21.660 --> 01:08:23.788
I really do enjoy
training hard, but that

01:08:23.788 --> 01:08:25.830
was something that I
learned how to do over time.

01:08:25.830 --> 01:08:28.680
I took on the mentality
that I'm here by choice,

01:08:28.680 --> 01:08:31.380
I'm here for my own
good and my own fitness

01:08:31.380 --> 01:08:34.812
to enhance my life so I'm
going to enjoy training hard,

01:08:34.812 --> 01:08:36.479
I'm going to enjoy
training effectively.

01:08:36.479 --> 01:08:39.021
And of course, there are days
when I train a little less hard

01:08:39.021 --> 01:08:40.140
or I back off quite a bit.

01:08:40.140 --> 01:08:42.330
I even take rest
periods of a week

01:08:42.330 --> 01:08:45.060
every once in a while,
every say 12 to 16 weeks

01:08:45.060 --> 01:08:47.930
I'll take a week off and just
do some activities like hiking

01:08:47.930 --> 01:08:48.930
and things of that sort.

01:08:48.930 --> 01:08:50.910
I talk to all about
extended layoffs,

01:08:50.910 --> 01:08:53.790
meaning a layoff of more than
two days during the episode

01:08:53.790 --> 01:08:57.029
that I did by myself, which is
the Optimal Fitness protocols

01:08:57.029 --> 01:08:57.750
episode.

01:08:57.750 --> 01:09:01.560
But in any case, learning to
train hard and enjoy training

01:09:01.560 --> 01:09:04.747
hard and really making
the workout something that

01:09:04.747 --> 01:09:06.330
is separate from the
rest of your life

01:09:06.330 --> 01:09:08.189
is one of the most
gratifying things

01:09:08.189 --> 01:09:11.640
that you can do to enhance
your overall fitness because it

01:09:11.640 --> 01:09:13.470
really teaches you
how to designate

01:09:13.470 --> 01:09:16.529
your mind and your body toward
this one specific set of goals

01:09:16.529 --> 01:09:18.930
while you are there
and to really enjoy

01:09:18.930 --> 01:09:21.240
the process because
fitness can be a truly

01:09:21.240 --> 01:09:23.529
enjoyable process even when
you are exerting yourself,

01:09:23.529 --> 01:09:24.520
especially hard.

01:09:24.520 --> 01:09:26.100
And for you
masochists out there,

01:09:26.100 --> 01:09:28.439
it can be, especially
because you're training hard

01:09:28.439 --> 01:09:29.640
that it feels so good.

01:09:29.640 --> 01:09:34.260
In any event, the key is to
set some sort of boundary

01:09:34.260 --> 01:09:36.720
and know that when you
cross into that boundary,

01:09:36.720 --> 01:09:37.540
you're training.

01:09:37.540 --> 01:09:39.207
And when you cross
out of that boundary,

01:09:39.207 --> 01:09:41.160
you're done training,
which also lends itself

01:09:41.160 --> 01:09:44.250
to more adequate recovery
and the decompression type

01:09:44.250 --> 01:09:46.272
breathing exercises that
we talked about before.

01:09:46.272 --> 01:09:47.939
I'm not going to tell
you whether or not

01:09:47.939 --> 01:09:49.290
you need to do the
down regulation

01:09:49.290 --> 01:09:51.457
breathing at the end of
your workout within the line

01:09:51.457 --> 01:09:52.691
or after you cross the line.

01:09:52.691 --> 01:09:53.399
That's up to you.

01:09:53.399 --> 01:09:55.410
I don't think one needs
to get that specific.

01:09:55.410 --> 01:09:57.720
Now, another tool that's
wonderfully effective

01:09:57.720 --> 01:10:00.570
not just for your workouts
but for all areas of your life

01:10:00.570 --> 01:10:04.410
is if you are going to bring
a smartphone to your workouts,

01:10:04.410 --> 01:10:07.950
to set some boundaries
around what you're

01:10:07.950 --> 01:10:10.710
going to listen to and
do with that smartphone

01:10:10.710 --> 01:10:12.060
during your workouts.

01:10:12.060 --> 01:10:13.350
I see people texting.

01:10:13.350 --> 01:10:14.610
I see people doing selfies.

01:10:14.610 --> 01:10:17.670
I see people having phone calls.

01:10:17.670 --> 01:10:21.540
I see people, I presume,
listening to music or podcasts.

01:10:21.540 --> 01:10:24.720
Look, I am not the smartphone
police nor are you,

01:10:24.720 --> 01:10:27.900
and everyone has a right to
use their smartphone in the way

01:10:27.900 --> 01:10:29.490
that they choose
as best for them

01:10:29.490 --> 01:10:31.950
in order to distract
themselves or focus themselves

01:10:31.950 --> 01:10:33.240
or enrich their life.

01:10:33.240 --> 01:10:35.550
Look, it's a free world,
of course, more for some

01:10:35.550 --> 01:10:37.420
than for others,
but you can do what

01:10:37.420 --> 01:10:38.670
you want with your smartphone.

01:10:38.670 --> 01:10:41.835
However, if your goal is
to improve your fitness,

01:10:41.835 --> 01:10:44.460
one of the more powerful things
you can do with your smartphone

01:10:44.460 --> 01:10:49.080
is to decide before you cross
the line into your workout what

01:10:49.080 --> 01:10:52.180
you're going to listen to or
do with that phone or not.

01:10:52.180 --> 01:10:55.380
So for me, I like to
designate a playlist of music

01:10:55.380 --> 01:10:57.400
for that particular
workout, and then

01:10:57.400 --> 01:10:58.650
I just stick to that playlist.

01:10:58.650 --> 01:11:00.780
I might repeat songs
that I like a lot,

01:11:00.780 --> 01:11:03.090
or if someone talks to me
while the music is playing,

01:11:03.090 --> 01:11:05.520
I might go back and restart
a song if they distracted me,

01:11:05.520 --> 01:11:06.312
that sort of thing.

01:11:06.312 --> 01:11:09.060
Although, I do my best to not
get into too much social chit

01:11:09.060 --> 01:11:11.490
chat during workouts,
but I'm friendly,

01:11:11.490 --> 01:11:13.573
and it's nice when people
come over and say hello.

01:11:13.573 --> 01:11:15.740
I sometimes work out with
other people in which case

01:11:15.740 --> 01:11:17.940
I don't use headphones,
I don't use a smartphone.

01:11:17.940 --> 01:11:23.730
But setting a playlist or two,
designating a podcast or two,

01:11:23.730 --> 01:11:26.220
designating an audiobook
or two, whatever

01:11:26.220 --> 01:11:28.770
it is that you're going to
listen to really decide what

01:11:28.770 --> 01:11:31.000
that's going to be before
you do your workout.

01:11:31.000 --> 01:11:33.930
And the reason I say this is
that I observe a lot of people,

01:11:33.930 --> 01:11:38.220
and frankly, I've observed
myself under conditions where

01:11:38.220 --> 01:11:40.680
I'm suddenly in a
text communication,

01:11:40.680 --> 01:11:44.550
or I'm bouncing between
albums or between podcasts

01:11:44.550 --> 01:11:47.130
or between whatever it is
on the phone to the point

01:11:47.130 --> 01:11:49.380
where rest intervals aren't
being controlled well,

01:11:49.380 --> 01:11:51.725
to the point where
focus during sets

01:11:51.725 --> 01:11:53.850
becomes harder to achieve
at the beginning of a set

01:11:53.850 --> 01:11:56.460
because in between sets I was
focused on a conversation not

01:11:56.460 --> 01:11:57.300
on training.

01:11:57.300 --> 01:12:00.330
I'm a big believer in
making your exercise fun,

01:12:00.330 --> 01:12:02.670
making it accessible,
meaning not so

01:12:02.670 --> 01:12:04.560
expensive or
geographically difficult

01:12:04.560 --> 01:12:07.710
to achieve that you don't do it
or that it starts to interfere

01:12:07.710 --> 01:12:08.910
with other areas of life.

01:12:08.910 --> 01:12:09.790
This is really important.

01:12:09.790 --> 01:12:12.207
You want fitness to be blended
with the rest of your life,

01:12:12.207 --> 01:12:14.760
but you don't want it so blended
with the rest of your life

01:12:14.760 --> 01:12:17.610
that the rest of your life
starts to impede your efforts.

01:12:17.610 --> 01:12:20.340
Or and this happens quite
often for a lot of people

01:12:20.340 --> 01:12:23.140
that workouts start to
take an hour and a half,

01:12:23.140 --> 01:12:25.933
two hours when they could easily
be completed in 45 minutes

01:12:25.933 --> 01:12:28.350
to an hour if you were just
more efficient with your time.

01:12:28.350 --> 01:12:30.433
And of course, you don't
need me to tell you this,

01:12:30.433 --> 01:12:34.320
but smartphones can be one of
the major bleeds on our focus

01:12:34.320 --> 01:12:35.170
and efficiency.

01:12:35.170 --> 01:12:37.440
In fact, it can cause
you to hemorrhage

01:12:37.440 --> 01:12:39.040
focus and efficiency.

01:12:39.040 --> 01:12:40.523
So what I'm
suggesting here is not

01:12:40.523 --> 01:12:42.690
throwing away your smartphone,
although, some people

01:12:42.690 --> 01:12:44.670
do benefit from just
leaving it in the car

01:12:44.670 --> 01:12:46.350
or at home when
they are training.

01:12:46.350 --> 01:12:50.160
But rather to designate
podcasts, books, music

01:12:50.160 --> 01:12:52.350
playlists for that
particular workout

01:12:52.350 --> 01:12:55.260
and to just stick to those for
the duration of your workout.

01:12:55.260 --> 01:12:57.210
And once you cross
into the line,

01:12:57.210 --> 01:13:00.420
that's what you're listening
to and only that or nothing.

01:13:00.420 --> 01:13:02.730
And of course, once you
cross back over the line

01:13:02.730 --> 01:13:04.977
as you finish your
workout, you can

01:13:04.977 --> 01:13:06.810
decide to continue to
listen to the podcast,

01:13:06.810 --> 01:13:09.143
or continue to listen to the
audiobook, or to the music.

01:13:09.143 --> 01:13:09.870
That's up to you.

01:13:09.870 --> 01:13:11.340
Although, I highly
recommend that you do

01:13:11.340 --> 01:13:13.080
incorporate that
downregulation period

01:13:13.080 --> 01:13:14.610
of 3 to 5 minutes minimum.

01:13:14.610 --> 01:13:17.520
The last category of tools
to improve your fitness

01:13:17.520 --> 01:13:21.280
come from the discussions about
nutrition and supplementation

01:13:21.280 --> 01:13:25.177
and recovery in the series
with Dr. Andy Galpin.

01:13:25.177 --> 01:13:27.010
Now, the list of tools
I'm about to describe

01:13:27.010 --> 01:13:29.290
is not exhaustive,
meaning it doesn't even

01:13:29.290 --> 01:13:32.387
begin to come close to
the total number of tools

01:13:32.387 --> 01:13:34.720
that one could glean from the
discussion about nutrition

01:13:34.720 --> 01:13:36.820
and supplementation
that I had with Dr. Andy

01:13:36.820 --> 01:13:40.030
Galpin on this podcast, but
they are the major ones that

01:13:40.030 --> 01:13:41.350
are definitely worth knowing.

01:13:41.350 --> 01:13:45.380
And those include supplementing
with omega 3 fatty acids.

01:13:45.380 --> 01:13:47.980
Now, omega 3 fatty acids
are found of course

01:13:47.980 --> 01:13:51.010
in foods, things like
fatty fish and krill,

01:13:51.010 --> 01:13:53.360
of all things, certain
forms of algae, et cetera.

01:13:53.360 --> 01:13:57.010
But most people do not get
enough of so-called EPA form

01:13:57.010 --> 01:13:57.607
of omega 3s.

01:13:57.607 --> 01:13:59.440
And for that reason, I
and many other people

01:13:59.440 --> 01:14:03.140
choose to supplement with
a minimum of 1 gram per day

01:14:03.140 --> 01:14:05.500
and in some cases as
high as 2 grams per day

01:14:05.500 --> 01:14:08.170
of omega 3s in supplement form.

01:14:08.170 --> 01:14:10.390
So typically one would
get to 1 to 2 grams

01:14:10.390 --> 01:14:13.900
of EPA by supplementing
their nutrition, their diet,

01:14:13.900 --> 01:14:17.640
that is, with fish oil
capsules or liquid fish oil.

01:14:17.640 --> 01:14:19.390
There are many different
sources of these.

01:14:19.390 --> 01:14:21.015
That was discussed
in an episode that I

01:14:21.015 --> 01:14:22.960
did with Dr. Rhonda Patrick.

01:14:22.960 --> 01:14:25.540
I find that it's
most cost efficient

01:14:25.540 --> 01:14:29.560
to get that 1 to 2 grams of
EPAs from liquid fish oil

01:14:29.560 --> 01:14:31.430
despite what you might
see on the internet.

01:14:31.430 --> 01:14:33.310
I don't have any
relationship whatsoever

01:14:33.310 --> 01:14:34.570
to a liquid fish oil company.

01:14:34.570 --> 01:14:37.390
You just want to make sure that
you go with a reputable brand.

01:14:37.390 --> 01:14:39.190
I like the ones
that are flavored

01:14:39.190 --> 01:14:43.030
with lemon so that it offsets
the taste of fish oil,

01:14:43.030 --> 01:14:45.950
and I'll take a tablespoon
or two of that per day.

01:14:45.950 --> 01:14:48.160
And if I'm traveling
and even if I'm not

01:14:48.160 --> 01:14:49.672
I will often use
fish oil capsules,

01:14:49.672 --> 01:14:51.880
and there are a variety of
different sources of those

01:14:51.880 --> 01:14:52.420
as well.

01:14:52.420 --> 01:14:54.520
Getting sufficient
amounts of omega 3

01:14:54.520 --> 01:14:56.860
has been shown to be
important for mood.

01:14:56.860 --> 01:14:59.920
So as a way to offset
depression but also

01:14:59.920 --> 01:15:02.740
for enhancing overall
mood that probably

01:15:02.740 --> 01:15:06.370
relates to the omega 3s
effect on neurotransmission,

01:15:06.370 --> 01:15:09.010
not just for neuromodulators
like serotonin and dopamine

01:15:09.010 --> 01:15:10.990
but for all neurotransmission.

01:15:10.990 --> 01:15:12.710
And neurotransmission,
of course,

01:15:12.710 --> 01:15:14.770
is essential for
neuromuscular performance.

01:15:14.770 --> 01:15:16.900
And the omega 3s
have been implicated

01:15:16.900 --> 01:15:19.530
in reducing the
inflammation response,

01:15:19.530 --> 01:15:21.450
cardiovascular
health, et cetera.

01:15:21.450 --> 01:15:23.920
I realized that there is
some debate about omega 3s,

01:15:23.920 --> 01:15:27.450
but when I look at the bulk of
literature about the omega 3s,

01:15:27.450 --> 01:15:29.550
it's very clear
to me that getting

01:15:29.550 --> 01:15:33.360
1 to 2 grams of EPA
form of omega 3 per day

01:15:33.360 --> 01:15:35.460
is the right thing for me to do.

01:15:35.460 --> 01:15:37.240
And many others
find that as well.

01:15:37.240 --> 01:15:38.910
The second tool to
enhance your fitness

01:15:38.910 --> 01:15:41.220
under this category of
nutrition and supplementation

01:15:41.220 --> 01:15:42.240
is creatine.

01:15:42.240 --> 01:15:44.880
Now, again, creatine is not
just found in supplement form.

01:15:44.880 --> 01:15:47.730
It's also found, of course, in
foods, in particular red meat.

01:15:47.730 --> 01:15:49.590
However, the amount
of red meat that one

01:15:49.590 --> 01:15:52.710
would have to eat in order
to get the amount of creatine

01:15:52.710 --> 01:15:55.440
that one would start to see
a real performance enhancing

01:15:55.440 --> 01:15:57.120
effect is just far too high.

01:15:57.120 --> 01:16:00.090
You'd be ingesting far too much
of other things in red meat

01:16:00.090 --> 01:16:02.520
that you wouldn't
want that much of.

01:16:02.520 --> 01:16:04.830
And for that reason, I
and many other people

01:16:04.830 --> 01:16:06.750
will take creatine daily.

01:16:06.750 --> 01:16:09.690
We now know there's no need
to so-called load creatinine

01:16:09.690 --> 01:16:11.500
in the old days as it were.

01:16:11.500 --> 01:16:14.223
So old days, by the way,
meaning mid '90s and 2000s,

01:16:14.223 --> 01:16:16.140
we were all told that
we had to load creatine,

01:16:16.140 --> 01:16:18.570
we had to take high-dose
creatine for four or five days

01:16:18.570 --> 01:16:20.845
and then you could back
off to a maintenance dose.

01:16:20.845 --> 01:16:23.470
Now it's very clear you can just
take a daily dose of creatine.

01:16:23.470 --> 01:16:24.845
And that it really
doesn't matter

01:16:24.845 --> 01:16:26.140
when you take that creatine.

01:16:26.140 --> 01:16:28.135
You can take it post-workout
as many people do.

01:16:28.135 --> 01:16:29.260
You can take it preworkout.

01:16:29.260 --> 01:16:30.920
It really doesn't
seem to matter.

01:16:30.920 --> 01:16:34.060
I happen to take it postworkout
just as a matter of habit.

01:16:34.060 --> 01:16:36.280
But again, you can take
it any time of day.

01:16:36.280 --> 01:16:38.200
Now, the point I want
to make about creatine

01:16:38.200 --> 01:16:40.390
is one that's a bit different
than the other discussions

01:16:40.390 --> 01:16:40.890
out there.

01:16:40.890 --> 01:16:42.760
I have no issue
with the majority

01:16:42.760 --> 01:16:44.710
of what's discussed
about creatine out there,

01:16:44.710 --> 01:16:46.735
for instance, that
creatine monohydrate

01:16:46.735 --> 01:16:47.860
is the most effective form.

01:16:47.860 --> 01:16:49.510
Fortunately,
creatine monohydrate

01:16:49.510 --> 01:16:51.790
is also the least
expensive form of creatine

01:16:51.790 --> 01:16:52.930
that's sold out there.

01:16:52.930 --> 01:16:55.480
I see no evidence whatsoever
that the other forms

01:16:55.480 --> 01:16:58.180
of creatine are superior
to creatine monohydrate.

01:16:58.180 --> 01:17:01.810
But what you'll usually
hear is that taking

01:17:01.810 --> 01:17:06.310
5 grams of creatine monohydrate
per day is ideal for everybody.

01:17:06.310 --> 01:17:08.470
And that advice is
simply not well-informed

01:17:08.470 --> 01:17:09.850
by the scientific literature.

01:17:09.850 --> 01:17:13.390
If you are a larger person,
so for instance I weigh 100kg

01:17:13.390 --> 01:17:15.855
so that's about 220
pounds, well, it

01:17:15.855 --> 01:17:17.480
turns out if you look
at the literature

01:17:17.480 --> 01:17:19.440
on creatine and
athletic performance,

01:17:19.440 --> 01:17:20.870
and if you look
at the literature

01:17:20.870 --> 01:17:22.820
on creatine and
cognitive performance,

01:17:22.820 --> 01:17:24.710
because as some of
you already know,

01:17:24.710 --> 01:17:28.250
creatine is a fuel or the
phosphocreatine system

01:17:28.250 --> 01:17:31.530
is a fuel system for
the brain as well.

01:17:31.530 --> 01:17:34.610
And if you look at the
studies on creatine,

01:17:34.610 --> 01:17:37.220
they almost always gauge
the amount of creatine

01:17:37.220 --> 01:17:39.660
to give an individual
based on their body weight.

01:17:39.660 --> 01:17:42.050
So you don't have to get
really specific about this,

01:17:42.050 --> 01:17:46.820
but if you weigh, say,
185 pounds to 250 pounds,

01:17:46.820 --> 01:17:49.280
you can get away with
and probably should

01:17:49.280 --> 01:17:51.840
be taking 10 grams or
so of creatine per day,

01:17:51.840 --> 01:17:52.800
which is what I do.

01:17:52.800 --> 01:17:55.910
Whereas if you weigh less
than that, 5 grams or maybe

01:17:55.910 --> 01:17:57.780
even 3 grams is sufficient.

01:17:57.780 --> 01:18:00.525
Now, I discussed this with Dr.
Andy Galpin during that series,

01:18:00.525 --> 01:18:02.150
and one of the things
that I've started

01:18:02.150 --> 01:18:04.190
to do since the
closure of that series

01:18:04.190 --> 01:18:06.180
is to take more
creatine per day.

01:18:06.180 --> 01:18:08.030
So now I'm taking
10, sometimes even

01:18:08.030 --> 01:18:10.370
as much as 15 grams
per day of creatine.

01:18:10.370 --> 01:18:12.620
Again, this is powdered
creatine monohydrate.

01:18:12.620 --> 01:18:14.930
My stomach tolerates
it very well,

01:18:14.930 --> 01:18:17.490
but frankly, I don't
tend to get stomach aches

01:18:17.490 --> 01:18:20.310
or gastric distress from
pretty much anything,

01:18:20.310 --> 01:18:23.400
unless it's some form
of food poisoning, which

01:18:23.400 --> 01:18:24.940
is exceedingly rare for me.

01:18:24.940 --> 01:18:27.930
So some people out there
find that creatine really

01:18:27.930 --> 01:18:30.180
disrupts their gut, and they
need to take it with food

01:18:30.180 --> 01:18:32.003
or they really need
to slowly and increase

01:18:32.003 --> 01:18:34.170
the amount of creatine that
they're taking each day.

01:18:34.170 --> 01:18:36.840
I find that I can put 10
even 15 grams of creatine

01:18:36.840 --> 01:18:41.025
into a whey protein
shake or into some water

01:18:41.025 --> 01:18:42.400
with a little bit
of lemon juice,

01:18:42.400 --> 01:18:44.250
just to make it taste a little
less chalky, drink that,

01:18:44.250 --> 01:18:46.210
and I don't have any
gastric distress from that.

01:18:46.210 --> 01:18:47.700
So you'll need to find
what works for you.

01:18:47.700 --> 01:18:49.950
But the point here is if
you're going to take creatine,

01:18:49.950 --> 01:18:51.492
you don't just want
to quote unquote,

01:18:51.492 --> 01:18:53.430
"take creatine one
scoop per day."

01:18:53.430 --> 01:18:55.680
You really want to adjust
the amount of creatine

01:18:55.680 --> 01:18:58.110
that you're ingesting
according to your body weight.

01:18:58.110 --> 01:19:01.620
And I would give you a very
specific formula of x grams

01:19:01.620 --> 01:19:04.590
of creatine per kilogram
or pound of body weight,

01:19:04.590 --> 01:19:07.620
but believe it or not, no
such specific recommendation

01:19:07.620 --> 01:19:10.200
has ever been published in
the scientific literature

01:19:10.200 --> 01:19:12.773
or at least I couldn't find
it in a way that's consistent

01:19:12.773 --> 01:19:14.190
with all the other
papers, meaning

01:19:14.190 --> 01:19:15.730
you see a lot of variation.

01:19:15.730 --> 01:19:19.710
So what I'm talking about here
is if you weigh 185 pounds

01:19:19.710 --> 01:19:23.400
or so, OK, plus or minus 5
pounds out to about 250 pounds,

01:19:23.400 --> 01:19:26.220
10 to 15g of creatine
per day is probably

01:19:26.220 --> 01:19:28.590
more appropriate for
you than is 5 grams,

01:19:28.590 --> 01:19:31.285
meaning it's going to be
more effective for enhancing

01:19:31.285 --> 01:19:32.160
physical performance.

01:19:32.160 --> 01:19:35.680
And perhaps again, perhaps even
cognitive performance as well.

01:19:35.680 --> 01:19:39.630
And if you're somebody
who weighs 180 pounds down

01:19:39.630 --> 01:19:42.720
to say 130 pounds, 5
grams of creatine per day

01:19:42.720 --> 01:19:44.100
is probably sufficient.

01:19:44.100 --> 01:19:46.680
The point here is if you
are taking creatine, again,

01:19:46.680 --> 01:19:48.150
not everyone has
to take creatine.

01:19:48.150 --> 01:19:50.547
There's no law that says that
you have to take creatine.

01:19:50.547 --> 01:19:51.630
Some people don't like it.

01:19:51.630 --> 01:19:52.740
I know some people
fear it's going

01:19:52.740 --> 01:19:53.730
to make their hair fall out.

01:19:53.730 --> 01:19:55.860
We already talked about
that in previous episodes

01:19:55.860 --> 01:19:58.380
and the lack of data
to support that idea.

01:19:58.380 --> 01:20:00.060
But I realize some
people steer away

01:20:00.060 --> 01:20:02.080
from creatine for
whatever reason.

01:20:02.080 --> 01:20:04.920
But if you decide that taking
creatine is right for you,

01:20:04.920 --> 01:20:06.540
adjust the total
amount of creatine

01:20:06.540 --> 01:20:08.820
that you take according
to your body weight.

01:20:08.820 --> 01:20:11.730
The next supplementation based
tool for enhancing your fitness

01:20:11.730 --> 01:20:14.130
is a Rhodiola rosea.

01:20:14.130 --> 01:20:16.260
Now, this very esoteric
sounding supplement

01:20:16.260 --> 01:20:19.290
is one that I learned about,
both from Dr. Lane Norton when

01:20:19.290 --> 01:20:21.660
he was a guest on this
podcast, expert in nutrition

01:20:21.660 --> 01:20:25.380
and frankly training as it
relates to resistance training,

01:20:25.380 --> 01:20:27.930
and from Dr. Andy Galpin.

01:20:27.930 --> 01:20:30.240
Rhodiola rosea is
a supplement that's

01:20:30.240 --> 01:20:33.030
gaining increasing attention
because it is what's

01:20:33.030 --> 01:20:34.860
called a cortisol modulator.

01:20:34.860 --> 01:20:37.620
It does not necessarily
suppress cortisol.

01:20:37.620 --> 01:20:39.810
It does not increase cortisol.

01:20:39.810 --> 01:20:41.460
It's a cortisol modulator.

01:20:41.460 --> 01:20:43.500
And frankly, the
mechanism by which

01:20:43.500 --> 01:20:45.840
Rhodiola rosea
modulates cortisol

01:20:45.840 --> 01:20:47.740
is still under investigation.

01:20:47.740 --> 01:20:49.680
I hope to do an episode
about it in the future

01:20:49.680 --> 01:20:51.450
or at least make it
part of an episode

01:20:51.450 --> 01:20:54.300
because the hypothesized
mechanism that's

01:20:54.300 --> 01:20:57.150
starting to emerge is really
interesting as it relates

01:20:57.150 --> 01:21:00.300
to neurons in the brain that
control the stress response

01:21:00.300 --> 01:21:02.430
and glands in the body
like the adrenals that

01:21:02.430 --> 01:21:05.250
control the stress response
and that secrete cortisol.

01:21:05.250 --> 01:21:08.040
Regardless, there's a
growing body of research

01:21:08.040 --> 01:21:12.660
that has explored Rhodiola
rosea supplementation and one's

01:21:12.660 --> 01:21:16.320
subjective perception
of fatigue or output

01:21:16.320 --> 01:21:18.840
during high-intensity
training of various kinds,

01:21:18.840 --> 01:21:22.110
both resistance training as well
as running and endurance type

01:21:22.110 --> 01:21:22.950
training.

01:21:22.950 --> 01:21:27.240
So I started taking Rhodiola
rosea about six months ago

01:21:27.240 --> 01:21:30.390
in response to conversations
that I had again with Dr. Lane

01:21:30.390 --> 01:21:33.450
Norton and with Dr.
Andy Galpin, and it's

01:21:33.450 --> 01:21:36.480
a supplement that I take
before high-intensity workouts.

01:21:36.480 --> 01:21:39.240
So I don't take it before a
run because frankly my runs are

01:21:39.240 --> 01:21:41.730
either very long
and slow, or they're

01:21:41.730 --> 01:21:44.580
very brief like a high-intensity
interval training session.

01:21:44.580 --> 01:21:47.453
And I find those to be
pretty easy to recover from

01:21:47.453 --> 01:21:48.870
even though they
are very intense.

01:21:48.870 --> 01:21:51.930
I might take a Rhodiola
rosea supplement

01:21:51.930 --> 01:21:55.440
before doing a 30-minute
hill run that's very intense.

01:21:55.440 --> 01:21:58.830
But typically, I only take
it about 10 to 15 minutes

01:21:58.830 --> 01:22:01.350
before any sort of
high-intensity resistance

01:22:01.350 --> 01:22:03.150
training session,
in particular my leg

01:22:03.150 --> 01:22:06.930
day which falls on day 2
of my exercise protocol,

01:22:06.930 --> 01:22:10.050
or the torso day, or the
small body parts day.

01:22:10.050 --> 01:22:12.330
Again, here I'm
referencing the way

01:22:12.330 --> 01:22:15.180
that I train across the week,
and you can find that training

01:22:15.180 --> 01:22:17.680
protocol as a downloadable
completely zero-cost

01:22:17.680 --> 01:22:18.310
if you like.

01:22:18.310 --> 01:22:20.710
But I realize other people
are using different body

01:22:20.710 --> 01:22:23.260
part splits and different
combinations of resistance

01:22:23.260 --> 01:22:25.450
training and endurance training.

01:22:25.450 --> 01:22:28.060
The reason I mentioned
Rhodiola rosea in this episode

01:22:28.060 --> 01:22:30.910
is that I realized that while
some people might not yet

01:22:30.910 --> 01:22:34.360
be supplementing omega 3s,
they might not be supplementing

01:22:34.360 --> 01:22:37.030
creatine, there are many
of you who are already

01:22:37.030 --> 01:22:39.550
doing those things, and you're
looking for additional tools

01:22:39.550 --> 01:22:40.420
to give you an edge.

01:22:40.420 --> 01:22:42.490
So again, the Rhodiola
rosea would not

01:22:42.490 --> 01:22:44.633
fall into the category of
foundational supplements.

01:22:44.633 --> 01:22:47.050
Certainly, get your nutrition
right, get your sleep right,

01:22:47.050 --> 01:22:47.800
get your sunlight.

01:22:47.800 --> 01:22:49.450
All the basics first
please before even

01:22:49.450 --> 01:22:51.070
thinking about any supplements.

01:22:51.070 --> 01:22:54.250
However, once you get into
the category of supplements

01:22:54.250 --> 01:22:56.950
that can enhance
fitness, Rhodiola rosea

01:22:56.950 --> 01:22:58.660
does seem to have
some good research

01:22:58.660 --> 01:23:00.520
to support it in
the context of lots

01:23:00.520 --> 01:23:03.050
of different forms of
high-intensity exercise.

01:23:03.050 --> 01:23:06.100
Now, I can't tell you whether
or not it's purely subjective

01:23:06.100 --> 01:23:08.890
or whether or not it's
objective and subjective,

01:23:08.890 --> 01:23:12.850
but my experience has been
that when I take Rhodiola rosea

01:23:12.850 --> 01:23:15.850
I definitely notice
that I can exert myself

01:23:15.850 --> 01:23:18.650
harder without feeling
like I'm bringing myself

01:23:18.650 --> 01:23:21.650
to the brink of fatigue
either during the exertion

01:23:21.650 --> 01:23:22.730
or afterwards.

01:23:22.730 --> 01:23:24.860
In other words,
I feel like I can

01:23:24.860 --> 01:23:27.890
do more work without
feeling so exhausted,

01:23:27.890 --> 01:23:30.830
and I feel as if I'm
recovering from my workouts

01:23:30.830 --> 01:23:33.320
more quickly, in
particular across the day

01:23:33.320 --> 01:23:34.580
after my workouts.

01:23:34.580 --> 01:23:37.640
In fact, if I had to cite one
specific subjective effect

01:23:37.640 --> 01:23:39.650
that I've experienced
from taking Rhodiola rosea

01:23:39.650 --> 01:23:42.740
before very high-intensity
workouts is that prior

01:23:42.740 --> 01:23:46.630
to taking it, I would
often find that 3 or 4

01:23:46.630 --> 01:23:48.440
hours after the
workout having eaten

01:23:48.440 --> 01:23:52.100
a good meal, taking a shower,
et cetera, and I was tired.

01:23:52.100 --> 01:23:53.840
I'd have a real dip in energy.

01:23:53.840 --> 01:23:55.688
But now I notice that
I have a lot of energy

01:23:55.688 --> 01:23:57.980
throughout the day even after
these very high-intensity

01:23:57.980 --> 01:24:00.020
sessions in the early
part of the day.

01:24:00.020 --> 01:24:02.300
And frankly, I haven't
changed anything else

01:24:02.300 --> 01:24:04.880
about my supplementation
or my nutrition, at least

01:24:04.880 --> 01:24:06.140
nothing major.

01:24:06.140 --> 01:24:07.940
So I personally am
going to continue

01:24:07.940 --> 01:24:10.610
to take Rhodiola rosea before
these high-intensity workouts.

01:24:10.610 --> 01:24:13.200
So for me, that's about two
or three times per week.

01:24:13.200 --> 01:24:15.290
However, if I forgot
to take Rhodiola rosea

01:24:15.290 --> 01:24:17.000
before a workout,
I have no reason

01:24:17.000 --> 01:24:19.070
to think that workout
would go much worse.

01:24:19.070 --> 01:24:22.340
This is a supplement that is
designed to give you an edge

01:24:22.340 --> 01:24:25.340
to be able to exert
more focus and intensity

01:24:25.340 --> 01:24:28.010
during your workouts with
less perceived exertion

01:24:28.010 --> 01:24:29.660
and to enhance your recovery.

01:24:29.660 --> 01:24:31.340
The typical dosage
of Rhodiola rosea

01:24:31.340 --> 01:24:32.840
that you'll find
in most supplements

01:24:32.840 --> 01:24:35.297
is 100 to 200 milligrams.

01:24:35.297 --> 01:24:37.880
And of course, any time you're
going to take a new supplement,

01:24:37.880 --> 01:24:41.445
you would be wise to figure
out the lowest effective dose

01:24:41.445 --> 01:24:42.320
from that supplement.

01:24:42.320 --> 01:24:44.300
That's just logic, right?

01:24:44.300 --> 01:24:46.190
Why spend more money
taking more of something

01:24:46.190 --> 01:24:48.232
that you don't need more
of if you could get away

01:24:48.232 --> 01:24:50.630
with taking less of it,
and it's just as effective

01:24:50.630 --> 01:24:51.960
maybe even more effective?

01:24:51.960 --> 01:24:54.440
So I typically will take
100 to 200 milligrams

01:24:54.440 --> 01:24:58.190
of Rhodiola rosea about 10 to
20 minutes before a workout.

01:24:58.190 --> 01:25:00.710
However, I've taken as
little as 100 milligrams

01:25:00.710 --> 01:25:02.900
on a consistent basis, and
frankly, I don't really

01:25:02.900 --> 01:25:05.750
experience much difference
whether I take 100mg

01:25:05.750 --> 01:25:07.640
or I take 200 milligrams
before a workout,

01:25:07.640 --> 01:25:11.000
so lately I've just defaulted
to taking 100 milligrams

01:25:11.000 --> 01:25:14.030
of Rhodiola rosea before
any high-intensity workout.

01:25:14.030 --> 01:25:15.800
Now, the final tool
that I want to review

01:25:15.800 --> 01:25:19.970
for improving your fitness comes
from the category of nutrition.

01:25:19.970 --> 01:25:22.220
I've done lots of
episodes about nutrition

01:25:22.220 --> 01:25:23.543
already on this podcast.

01:25:23.543 --> 01:25:25.460
We've done episodes about
intermittent fasting

01:25:25.460 --> 01:25:29.630
I did a long interview
episode with Dr. Lane Norton

01:25:29.630 --> 01:25:32.720
where we discussed all the
ins and outs of nutrition

01:25:32.720 --> 01:25:36.890
as it relates to fat
loss, muscle gain, fitness

01:25:36.890 --> 01:25:38.790
in general,
lifestyle in general.

01:25:38.790 --> 01:25:41.432
So check out that episode where
you will learn his philosophy

01:25:41.432 --> 01:25:43.640
on nutrition, which frankly
is the one that I largely

01:25:43.640 --> 01:25:44.390
subscribe to.

01:25:44.390 --> 01:25:47.270
And of course, obeys the laws
of thermodynamics, calories

01:25:47.270 --> 01:25:49.850
in, calories out being
fundamentally important.

01:25:49.850 --> 01:25:52.610
But also gets into all sorts
of details about which sources

01:25:52.610 --> 01:25:54.680
of protein are most
effective and bioavailable,

01:25:54.680 --> 01:25:58.040
how much protein you can
incorporate into your muscles

01:25:58.040 --> 01:26:00.140
after training, et
cetera, all of that

01:26:00.140 --> 01:26:02.060
is included in that episode.

01:26:02.060 --> 01:26:05.360
With that said, the series on
exercise with Dr. Andy Galpin

01:26:05.360 --> 01:26:08.000
also included an
episode on nutrition.

01:26:08.000 --> 01:26:10.020
And while having the
discussion for that episode

01:26:10.020 --> 01:26:11.930
and then listening to
that episode again,

01:26:11.930 --> 01:26:15.740
I realized that while certainly
I've gotten a number of things

01:26:15.740 --> 01:26:17.960
right about my nutrition
across the years,

01:26:17.960 --> 01:26:21.380
there are a few areas where
I could probably do better

01:26:21.380 --> 01:26:24.020
without much effort in
ways that could really

01:26:24.020 --> 01:26:25.430
enhance my fitness.

01:26:25.430 --> 01:26:26.990
And the thing that
I'm referring to

01:26:26.990 --> 01:26:29.420
is that for me my first
meal of the day laying

01:26:29.420 --> 01:26:31.773
somewhere around 11:00
AM maybe 12:00 noon.

01:26:31.773 --> 01:26:33.440
Sometimes I'll eat
an earlier breakfast,

01:26:33.440 --> 01:26:36.680
but most typically I hydrate,
caffeinate, and train in

01:26:36.680 --> 01:26:40.170
the morning, and then I eat
some time around 11:00 or 12:00.

01:26:40.170 --> 01:26:41.840
And then I eat my
last meal of the day

01:26:41.840 --> 01:26:43.910
sometime around 8:30 or 9:00.

01:26:43.910 --> 01:26:47.910
And as some of you already know,
I tend to organize my meals,

01:26:47.910 --> 01:26:50.420
such that meals during
the early part of the day

01:26:50.420 --> 01:26:54.440
tend to lean more toward protein
and fibrous carbohydrates,

01:26:54.440 --> 01:26:58.190
so things like meat and salad,
or chicken and salad, fish

01:26:58.190 --> 01:27:00.320
and salad, and maybe a
little bit of starch.

01:27:00.320 --> 01:27:02.210
And the meals that I
eat later in the day

01:27:02.210 --> 01:27:05.510
tend to be more starch focused
and more vegetable focused

01:27:05.510 --> 01:27:08.147
or things like pasta, rice,
et cetera, later in the day

01:27:08.147 --> 01:27:09.230
because it helps me sleep.

01:27:09.230 --> 01:27:11.000
And the architecture
of all that is really

01:27:11.000 --> 01:27:12.260
about energy and focus.

01:27:12.260 --> 01:27:15.050
I find I can focus a bit
better and I have more energy

01:27:15.050 --> 01:27:17.970
throughout the day when I have
my first meal at around 11:00

01:27:17.970 --> 01:27:20.770
or 12:00, and I keep the
total amount of carbohydrates

01:27:20.770 --> 01:27:22.750
that I ingest during
the day moderate.

01:27:22.750 --> 01:27:24.670
Not low but moderate.

01:27:24.670 --> 01:27:26.210
Now, there is an
exception to that,

01:27:26.210 --> 01:27:28.588
which is if I do a
high-intensity resistance

01:27:28.588 --> 01:27:30.130
training session
early in the morning

01:27:30.130 --> 01:27:33.220
say train legs or train torso
or even small body parts early

01:27:33.220 --> 01:27:36.340
in the morning, then I make
sure to incorporate more starchy

01:27:36.340 --> 01:27:39.070
carbohydrates and some
fruit, some simple sugars

01:27:39.070 --> 01:27:41.230
as well into the
first meal of the day

01:27:41.230 --> 01:27:43.270
so that I can
replenish the glycogen

01:27:43.270 --> 01:27:45.700
that I depleted during those
high-intensity resistance

01:27:45.700 --> 01:27:46.940
training sessions.

01:27:46.940 --> 01:27:50.410
However, after talking
to Dr. Andy Galpin,

01:27:50.410 --> 01:27:53.890
I realized that I really
shouldn't worry about or be

01:27:53.890 --> 01:27:55.900
afraid of eating
something before training

01:27:55.900 --> 01:27:57.770
if I'm really hungry
in the morning.

01:27:57.770 --> 01:27:59.650
So what I'm
referring to here are

01:27:59.650 --> 01:28:02.500
the times in which I wake
up and I want to train,

01:28:02.500 --> 01:28:05.930
but I personally like to
train fasted and caffeinated.

01:28:05.930 --> 01:28:06.430
OK.

01:28:06.430 --> 01:28:09.490
Yes, I do recommend that people
delay their caffeine intake

01:28:09.490 --> 01:28:13.030
90 to 120 minutes after
waking if and only

01:28:13.030 --> 01:28:15.280
if you have trouble
with an afternoon

01:28:15.280 --> 01:28:17.440
crash, real fatigue
in the afternoon, then

01:28:17.440 --> 01:28:19.330
it makes sense to
delay your caffeine 90

01:28:19.330 --> 01:28:21.040
to 120 minutes after waking.

01:28:21.040 --> 01:28:23.677
However, the
exception to that is

01:28:23.677 --> 01:28:25.510
that if I'm going to
train early in the day,

01:28:25.510 --> 01:28:29.350
I do ingest water to hydrate
as well as electrolytes

01:28:29.350 --> 01:28:31.570
and caffeine prior to training.

01:28:31.570 --> 01:28:33.520
And sometimes that means
I'm drinking caffeine

01:28:33.520 --> 01:28:35.980
within 30 minutes or
60 minutes of waking.

01:28:35.980 --> 01:28:38.320
I've tried to be clear about
this in previous episodes,

01:28:38.320 --> 01:28:40.030
but I think a number
of people have

01:28:40.030 --> 01:28:42.910
come to think that I
always delay my caffeine

01:28:42.910 --> 01:28:44.738
intake 90 to 120
minutes after waking,

01:28:44.738 --> 01:28:46.030
and that's simply not the case.

01:28:46.030 --> 01:28:47.822
If I'm going to train,
in particular if I'm

01:28:47.822 --> 01:28:49.480
going to do
high-intensity resistance

01:28:49.480 --> 01:28:53.230
training or a long run, I will
ingest caffeine sooner than

01:28:53.230 --> 01:28:55.480
90 to 120 minutes after waking.

01:28:55.480 --> 01:28:58.360
And in addition to
that, yes, I tend

01:28:58.360 --> 01:29:01.420
to eat my first meal around
11:00 AM maybe 12:00 noon.

01:29:01.420 --> 01:29:03.400
But if I wake up
and I'm very hungry,

01:29:03.400 --> 01:29:06.430
I will eat a small meal
that includes typically

01:29:06.430 --> 01:29:08.740
some protein and some fat,
so some Brazil nuts, maybe

01:29:08.740 --> 01:29:10.157
a couple of scoops
of whey protein

01:29:10.157 --> 01:29:12.220
would be typical for
me, or maybe even

01:29:12.220 --> 01:29:14.770
a little bit of oatmeal,
some whey protein,

01:29:14.770 --> 01:29:16.450
not a lot of food in my gut.

01:29:16.450 --> 01:29:19.810
But after talking to
Dr. Andy Galpin, what

01:29:19.810 --> 01:29:22.630
I learned was for some people
training fasted feels best.

01:29:22.630 --> 01:29:25.630
I would consider myself
one of those people.

01:29:25.630 --> 01:29:27.830
You may be somebody in
that category as well,

01:29:27.830 --> 01:29:29.650
or you might be
somebody who really

01:29:29.650 --> 01:29:32.650
feels as if you run
best, you resistance

01:29:32.650 --> 01:29:36.160
train best when you've eaten say
90 minutes or a couple of hours

01:29:36.160 --> 01:29:37.630
before you do that.

01:29:37.630 --> 01:29:39.910
There are basically
no specific rules

01:29:39.910 --> 01:29:43.480
as it relates to whether or not
you train fasted or train fed

01:29:43.480 --> 01:29:46.010
except in what you can handle
in terms of gastric distress.

01:29:46.010 --> 01:29:48.370
So you want to make food
choices according to that

01:29:48.370 --> 01:29:51.250
and try and avoid, of
course, gastric distress.

01:29:51.250 --> 01:29:54.790
But basically the change that
I've made is if I wake up

01:29:54.790 --> 01:29:56.470
and I'm hungry, I'll
eat a small meal,

01:29:56.470 --> 01:29:58.577
or if I want to work
out in the afternoon

01:29:58.577 --> 01:30:00.160
or I have to work
out in the afternoon

01:30:00.160 --> 01:30:04.930
and I have lunch at say,
12:00 or 12:30 or 11:00 AM

01:30:04.930 --> 01:30:07.750
and the only opportunity
that I have to train

01:30:07.750 --> 01:30:11.830
is 1:00 PM or even 12:30,
I will go ahead and train.

01:30:11.830 --> 01:30:13.600
And that's a new thing for me.

01:30:13.600 --> 01:30:15.610
Typically, I try
to keep my meals

01:30:15.610 --> 01:30:19.660
at least three to four hours
prior to any training bout.

01:30:19.660 --> 01:30:21.670
And of course, if you're
sleeping all night,

01:30:21.670 --> 01:30:23.680
you're not eating, and then if
you wake up and you don't eat

01:30:23.680 --> 01:30:25.480
and you train in the
morning, that's certainly

01:30:25.480 --> 01:30:27.730
longer than three or four
hours unless you're sleeping

01:30:27.730 --> 01:30:29.020
very, very little frankly.

01:30:29.020 --> 01:30:30.910
So essentially what I'm
saying is figure out

01:30:30.910 --> 01:30:32.080
what works best for you.

01:30:32.080 --> 01:30:34.120
Do you prefer to
train fasted or fed?

01:30:34.120 --> 01:30:37.960
For some of you, you might
prefer fasted before cardio

01:30:37.960 --> 01:30:39.880
and fed before
resistance training.

01:30:39.880 --> 01:30:43.310
For some of you, it might
be fasted is always best.

01:30:43.310 --> 01:30:44.950
Again, I put myself
in that category.

01:30:44.950 --> 01:30:47.740
For some of you, it might
be fed is always best.

01:30:47.740 --> 01:30:49.400
Again, this is
highly individual.

01:30:49.400 --> 01:30:51.650
And that's another point
that I'm trying to make here,

01:30:51.650 --> 01:30:54.820
which is Dr. Galpin really
impressed upon me that there

01:30:54.820 --> 01:30:58.060
is no hard and fast rule
about training fasted or fed.

01:30:58.060 --> 01:31:01.990
And, this is the second point,
that having some flexibility

01:31:01.990 --> 01:31:04.540
in whether or not you
can train fasted or fed

01:31:04.540 --> 01:31:06.700
allows you to incorporate
your fitness training

01:31:06.700 --> 01:31:09.370
sessions more readily
into a shifting schedule.

01:31:09.370 --> 01:31:11.770
And that's a really
overarching theme of everything

01:31:11.770 --> 01:31:14.020
we've been discussing
today, which is yes,

01:31:14.020 --> 01:31:17.200
it's wonderful and important
to have a core fitness

01:31:17.200 --> 01:31:19.180
program, something that
you're really striving

01:31:19.180 --> 01:31:20.440
to do each and every week.

01:31:20.440 --> 01:31:22.420
And for me, that's three
sessions of cardio,

01:31:22.420 --> 01:31:24.130
three resistance
training sessions,

01:31:24.130 --> 01:31:26.710
and a day where I'm doing
thermal stress training, which

01:31:26.710 --> 01:31:29.500
is just fancy language for
deliberate cold and deliberate

01:31:29.500 --> 01:31:30.350
heat exposure.

01:31:30.350 --> 01:31:35.690
However, real life happens,
travel, work, illness,

01:31:35.690 --> 01:31:37.330
family, all those
sorts of things

01:31:37.330 --> 01:31:39.160
that can impinge on
an exercise schedule

01:31:39.160 --> 01:31:41.890
and make it less likely that one
would complete their workouts.

01:31:41.890 --> 01:31:43.780
So today we've been
discussing tools

01:31:43.780 --> 01:31:48.280
to improve your fitness which
are brief, easy to incorporate,

01:31:48.280 --> 01:31:51.010
scientifically
supported, and that

01:31:51.010 --> 01:31:54.820
are shown to improve the various
sorts of exercise adaptations

01:31:54.820 --> 01:31:57.190
and recovery that will
allow you to get the most

01:31:57.190 --> 01:31:58.810
progress from your schedule.

01:31:58.810 --> 01:32:00.730
So while the tools
that we discussed today

01:32:00.730 --> 01:32:02.650
relate to breathing,
they relate to nutrition,

01:32:02.650 --> 01:32:04.150
they relate to
supplementation, they

01:32:04.150 --> 01:32:07.810
relate to specific set and
rep patterns and cadences

01:32:07.810 --> 01:32:09.700
and rest periods,
et cetera, all of

01:32:09.700 --> 01:32:13.390
those specific recommendations
are within a larger container

01:32:13.390 --> 01:32:16.340
that I hope has become clear,
which is the best tools

01:32:16.340 --> 01:32:18.810
to improve your fitness are
the tools that are, of course,

01:32:18.810 --> 01:32:20.450
are going to be
effective in improving

01:32:20.450 --> 01:32:24.390
your cardiovascular and strength
and hypertrophy training,

01:32:24.390 --> 01:32:26.480
et cetera, whatever it
is that your goals are,

01:32:26.480 --> 01:32:30.830
but also tools that are going to
make it easier and more likely

01:32:30.830 --> 01:32:33.230
that you are going to engage
in your fitness program

01:32:33.230 --> 01:32:36.470
with enthusiasm, with
effort, and with focus.

01:32:36.470 --> 01:32:38.880
And as with any episode
of this podcast,

01:32:38.880 --> 01:32:41.120
I covered a lot of
information, and there

01:32:41.120 --> 01:32:43.580
are a lot of different tools
that one could incorporate.

01:32:43.580 --> 01:32:46.400
By no means do you need
to incorporate them all.

01:32:46.400 --> 01:32:48.440
Although, if you choose
to, that's wonderful.

01:32:48.440 --> 01:32:50.630
Just even incorporating
one or two of them,

01:32:50.630 --> 01:32:53.180
say incorporating this notion
of the line and the exercise

01:32:53.180 --> 01:32:55.580
snacks, or adjusting
your level of flexibility

01:32:55.580 --> 01:32:58.340
as to whether or not you train
fasted or fed and the line,

01:32:58.340 --> 01:33:01.250
or trying a 12-week cycle of
purely training for strength

01:33:01.250 --> 01:33:02.840
when you do your
resistance training.

01:33:02.840 --> 01:33:05.720
But whether or not you pick
one tool or all the tools

01:33:05.720 --> 01:33:08.090
or somewhere in
between, the key thing

01:33:08.090 --> 01:33:09.770
is to actually implement them.

01:33:09.770 --> 01:33:12.170
And I like to think that
during today's discussion

01:33:12.170 --> 01:33:13.760
